The General settings Interface
•	The interface is visually organized into three principal areas: the status area, the navigation/header area, and the content area:
o	Status Bar: Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
	Time: Displays the local time as 3:56. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
	Dynamic Island: The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
	Connectivity & Power: The cellular signal strength icon displays two solid white bars and two gray bars, followed by the network type indicator ("LTE"). The adjacent battery icon appears partially filled alongside the digital readout "48."
o	Navigation & Header Bar: Establishing the user's hierarchical location within the iOS environment:
	Back-Navigation: The upper-left margin displays a back-navigation link labeled "Settings" accompanied by a directional chevron.
o	Interface Body:
	Introductory Module: Positioned at the upper portion of the viewport immediately below the navigation bar, presenting an introductory visual block composed of the following elements:
•	Icon Graphic: A solid gray rounded square containing a cog symbol.
•	Primary Heading: Centrally aligned or positioned directly adjacent, rendered in bold typography: "General".
•	Descriptive Text: Manage your overall setup and preferences for iPhone, such as software updates, device language, CarPlay, AirDrop, and more. 
	Visible Controls & Status Indicators (Initial View): Positioned immediately below the Introductory Module:
•	First module:
	About: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
	Software Update: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
	iPhone Storage: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
•	Second module:
	AppleCare & Warranty: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
•	Third module:
	AirDrop: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
	AirPlay & Continuity: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
	Pricture in Picture: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
	CarPlay: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
•	Fourth module:
	AutoFill & Passwords: Displayed as an interactive menu item.
